00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:01.990
I've heard the people

00:06:01.990 --> 00:06:03.545
that I work with, call
it almost body building

00:06:03.545 --> 00:06:04.500
for the heart.

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:06.550
As a doctor, I don't
quite like that statement

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:09.170
because an enlarged heart
is actually a bad heart.

00:06:09.170 --> 00:06:10.890
But, you want a stronger heart,

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:13.300
in that, it doesn't need to pump as often,

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:15.550
which allows it to calm down, relax,

00:06:15.550 --> 00:06:17.470
better improve filling time, all of that.

00:06:17.470 --> 00:06:19.200
And, we've seen better survival rates

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:21.110
through heart attacks, less heart attacks

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:22.730
when you have a lower resting heart rate.

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:24.210
Usually, that comes from exercise.

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:27.380
You could also, have a
low resting heart rate,

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:29.730
very low, that is
pathologic, meaning it's not

00:06:29.730 --> 00:06:31.830
because you exercise well and
you actually have a problem.

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:33.690
That's why we have the
term bradycardia for it,

00:06:33.690 --> 00:06:35.454
